From e0970e3d00796053f3c2f631e575a0d8943699a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:20:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] ci: merge-base jobs fetch commits only instead of
 fetch-depth 0 (#832)

* [daveey] ci: merge-base jobs fetch commits only instead of fetch-depth 0

prompt-surface-diff, lockfile-diff, history-check, contributor-check, lint's
ruff + ty diff and both supply-chain-audit jobs checked out with
fetch-depth: 0, which on this ~1 GB fork fetched all ~500 heads, every tag
and (mostly) every blob: 1m50s-3m on a good ci-fast runner and past the
job timeout on slow ones (#802, #806 3/3 attempts, sync PRs), failing
"All required checks pass (v2)".

They now keep the default depth-1 checkout and run the new
.github/actions/fetch-merge-base: one `git fetch --filter=tree:0
--unshallow` of HEAD and the base (branch or sha), commits only, no other
heads, no tags. History is complete, so merge-base, base..HEAD ranges and
git log --author answer exactly as on a full clone; trees and blobs of the
merge base load lazily on first use (blob:none promisor fetch, one batch per
tree). On the hub: 6-7 s for #806 vs a 9.6 s depth-1 checkout.
An empty merge base means unrelated histories; a fetch error fails the
step, so history-check never reads an error as "unrelated".

tests/ci/test_fetch_merge_base.py drives the script from a depth-1 clone
against a local origin: merge base and contributor log range equal a full
clone's (incl. a branch that merged main), lazy base reads, sha inputs the
checkout lacks, unrelated histories, and a fetch failure.

* [daveey] ci(fetch-merge-base): no expressions in the action description (the runner evaluates them)
